Concept of Operations (ConOps)
Automated Green Border Freight Corridor (AGBFC)
Operational Workflow for Semi-Trailer Processing
Version 0.1 (Draft)

1. Purpose
The purpose of this document is to define the operational workflow of an automated cross-border freight corridor connecting logistics hubs in Ukraine and Poland. The concept eliminates the need for tractor units and drivers to cross the border. Instead, semi-trailers are transported autonomously on electrically powered low-floor rail platforms between two logistics hubs.

The system is designed to:

eliminate long border queues;
reduce idle time of trucks and drivers;
minimize diesel fuel consumption and unnecessary engine idling;
improve freight turnover and transport efficiency;
enable continuous border inspection during transit;
reduce greenhouse gas emissions;
create a verifiable digital record of every transported semi-trailer.
2. Fundamental Principle
The transported object is not the truck.

The transported object is the identified freight unit (semi-trailer).

Only verified freight units are allowed to enter the transport corridor.

