16. Key Operational Principles
The proposed system is based on the following principles:

The semi-trailer is the primary transport entity.
Drivers and tractor units do not cross the border.
All freight units undergo automated inspection before entering the corridor.
Inspection data are merged into a single verified digital transport record.
The Decision Engine determines whether a trailer proceeds, is diverted, held, or rejected.
Secondary inspections are performed on dedicated inspection tracks without interrupting the main traffic flow.
Border-control procedures continue during transport rather than at a fixed border checkpoint.
Every operational event is recorded within the Digital Twin, ensuring complete traceability and supporting performance analysis, operational optimization, and environmental reporting.


